 Messages exist in English (`en`) and Korean (`ko`), in
 `src/i18n/messages.js`. The server answers in `LARDER_LANG` (default `en`).
+
+## Routes
+
+- `POST /import/sales`: accepts `{ "csv": "ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty\n..." }`.
+  Columns may be reordered. `ticket` is nonempty, `soldAt` is an ISO instant
+  with a timezone, `dishId` identifies a dish, and `qty` is positive with at
+  most three decimal places. Returns `{ "tickets": 1, "dishes": 2 }`, counting
+  newly imported tickets and the sum of their dish quantities. Every row of
+  a new ticket is imported; tickets from earlier imports are skipped.
+  Invalid rows or insufficient stock reject the entire file with a
+  `bad_request` message naming the physical CSV row (header is row 1).
+  Consumption is dated at `soldAt` with ledger ref `sale:<ticket>`.
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD`: returns an array of
+  `{ itemId, theoretical, actual, difference }` in item id order. Dates are
+  inclusive UTC days. Theoretical use is the ingredient snapshot from sales;
+  actual use includes every consume movement. Difference is actual minus
+  theoretical, rounded to three decimals. Only items with positive use appear.
