+## Sales (schema 3)
+
+- Schema 2 migrates to schema 3 by adding `sales: []` and `seq.sale: 0`.
+- Each sale has an id from `seq.sale`, ticket, normalized UTC `soldAt`, dishId,
+  qty, and an `ingredients` snapshot of scaled `{ itemId, qty }` requirements.
+  Historical theoretical use therefore survives recipe edits.
+- Ticket identity is global across imports. All rows of a new ticket are
+  stored together; subsequent imports skip that ticket. A failed file changes
+  neither sales, stock, ledger, nor sequences.
